a sacred place, considered a bridge between heaven and earth.

18
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:32,840
Now imagine a people who, with great difficulty, built a grandiose temple that practically

19
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:39,400
touched the sky... and, in a short time, saw it reduced to ashes by the flames of war.

20
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:46,400
In 586 BC, that is exactly what happened:

21
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:53,840
the Babylonians destroyed the Temple in Jerusalem and exiled the Jewish people. Centuries later,

22
00:02:53,840 --> 00:03:02,040
under Persian rule, the Jews returned and built a second, even larger temple.

23
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:07,600
This temple became the heart of the Jewish faith, until it was destroyed again by the

24
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:17,780
Romans in 70 AD, following a revolt. All that remained was a portion of its outer wall.

25
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:22,960
... For centuries, even scattered around

26
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:31,000
the world, Jews return to this place to pray, mourn, and keep their connection to

27
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:38,160
the sacred alive. Many know it as the Wailing Wall, but for the Jewish people

28
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:45,640
