of the Holy Sepulchre marks one of the holiest sites in Christianity; the Muslim Quarter,

62
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:51,240
the largest of all, filled with vibrant markets and centuries-old mosques; and the

63
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:58,440
Armenian Quarter, a reserved community, proud of its identity preserved for centuries.

64
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:04,560
Each space holds traditions, stories, and symbols that have shaped the destiny of the

65
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:08,720
city. ...

66
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:15,480
Located east of the Old City, the Mount of Olives is one of the

67
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:22,840
holiest sites in the world. Since ancient times, it has housed a Jewish cemetery

68
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:30,480
with more than 150,000 graves facing Jerusalem, symbolizing hope in the

69
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:34,880
resurrection. ...

70
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:42,560
For Christians, the mount was the scene of pivotal moments in Jesus' life,

71
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:49,160
such as the Garden of Gethsemane, the Church of All Nations, and the Chapel of the Ascension,

72
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:56,560
related to his ascension to heaven. ...

73
00:08:56,560 --> 00:09:03,200
In Islam, the mount is associated with the Day of Judgment, when a bridge will appear

74
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:09,400
leading the righteous to Paradise. ...

75
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:14,960
In addition to its religious significance, the mount offers a privileged view of

76
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:20,280
the Old City, with the Dome of the Rock and its golden walls as

77
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:23,960
prominent features. ...

78
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:32,120
In the 20th century, Jerusalem ceased to be merely a spiritual symbol and also became

79
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:42,200
