83
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:09,160
For many Jews, the hope of a future Third Temple remains alive. For Muslims,

84
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:15,520
on the other hand, the Temple Mount houses two of Islam's holiest sites,

85
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:21,960
making it an inviolable space. But beyond the walls,

86
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:27,640
in the stillness of the Palestinian hills, a birth would change the destiny of

87
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:32,920
humanity. …

88
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:41,960
This small town holds a great history. It was there that King David was born, and

89
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:51,820
according to sacred texts, it was from there that the Savior, for Christians, "Jesus Christ," would come.

90
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:59,000
… That is why Bethlehem is home to one of the

91
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:06,440
most venerated shrines of the Christian faith: the Church of the Nativity. Built in the 4th century by order

92
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:15,080
of Emperor Constantine, it was erected over the grotto where, according to tradition, Jesus was born. Today,

93
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:21,800
in addition to the historic altar, it houses the fourteen-pointed Silver Star that marks the exact spot

94
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:29,960
of Christ's birth. …

95
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:37,240
But Bethlehem does not live only from its biblical heritage. The city pulses with the still-living Palestinian culture,

96
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:44,840
in the meticulous olive wood carvings and traditional embroidery, steeped in history and

97
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:51,960
identity. But it is on the gray walls, erected by the conflict between Israel and Palestine, that

98
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:58,320
the city finds its most unexpected voice. ...

99
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:07,560
Banksy is a renowned British artist whose true identity remains a mystery.

100
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:13,680
Using the walls of the West Bank as canvases, especially in the Bethlehem region,

101
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:20,280
he has transformed concrete barriers into powerful symbols of resistance. Among his

102
