109
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:22,320
We now set out for the Judean Desert. We advance through a landscape of dry hills

110
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:29,480
and deep valleys, where silence has shaped refuges of faith among stones and

111
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:34,160
chasms. ...

112
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:42,640
Nestled on the cliffs of the Judean Desert, the Mar Saba Monastery is a

113
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:51,480
historic gem of the Christian faith. ...

114
00:13:51,480 --> 00:14:00,880
Located in the West Bank, about 15 kilometers from Bethlehem, it was founded in 483 AD

115
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:06,160
by Saint Saba, a monk considered a saint by the Greek Orthodox Church

116
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:10,560
of Jerusalem. ...

117
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:19,880
Its architecture, carved into the rocky hillside, blends with the desert landscape, creating an

118
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:28,000
almost surreal vision of the scenery. ...

119
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:34,440
Mar Saba was built to offer total isolation to the monks, who sought a life of

120
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:42,840
prayer, penance, and contemplation, far from the cities. Despite the adversities, Mar Saba

121
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:49,320
never interrupted its religious activities, keeping alive a monastic tradition that

122
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:55,720
